{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444062-cincinnatus-appropriate-inspiration-for-an-exalted-character","id":1444062,"title":"Cincinnatus: Appropriate Inspiration for an Exalted Character?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-15T13:35:35-07:00","id":1444062,"title":"Cincinnatus: Appropriate Inspiration for an Exalted Character?","content":"It seems like an obvious high-Integrity archetype, but a common refrain I recall from the 2e days was that Exaltation doesn't come to people who wouldn't use their power, and whole point of Cincinnatus is that he <i>does</i> step back from wielding power, so it seems to me that there's an inherent contradiction there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26529-anshu","name":"Anshu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26529_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T16:59:15-07:00","id":1444092,"title":"","content":"Not if he Exalts <i>during</i> his dictatorship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T18:12:24-07:00","id":1444113,"title":"","content":"Cinncinatus is DEFINITELY a fine inspiration for an Exalt. Dragon-blooded in particular is a slam dunk, the idea that a famous Dynast would come out of retirement to be awesome and then go back to her vineyard or ranch or whatever is super on-brand. The difference with a Celestial isn't that they wouldn't do it, it's that their &quot;prime&quot; lasts so long that the connotation is less &quot;retirement&quot; and more &quot;pursuing other interests for a while&quot;. But the basic idea that a Solar might lay low for a while and enjoy some hard-won R&amp;R for a decade or two isn't off base.<br /> <br /> If a Solar lives long enough to really retire, they're probably so powerful that coming out of retirement would require, and be, something Creation-shaping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 04-16-2021, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T19:08:42-07:00","id":1444121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anshu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444062-cincinnatus-appropriate-inspiration-for-an-exalted-character#post1444062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like an obvious high-Integrity archetype, but a common refrain I recall from the 2e days was that Exaltation doesn't come to people who wouldn't use their power, and whole point of Cincinnatus is that he <i>does</i> step back from wielding power, so it seems to me that there's an inherent contradiction there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Third Edition has softened that somewhat.<br /> <br /> It no longer requires a single driving goal at the core of the character replacing it with the concept of Essence Fever which is essentially that not using charms/essence isn't like being a wizard who can choose not to casting spells but more like an athlete who doesn't want to use their muscles. So you can disband your army and return to the farm until you're needed but if trouble comes near you you're probably not going to want to keep your head down because ultimately your essence wants to be used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T19:42:53-07:00","id":1444122,"title":"","content":"Must admit that, out of distraction, the ilustrous figure from roman history i initially thought of was <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incitatus\" target=\"_blank\">another</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T13:19:35-07:00","id":1444249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444062-cincinnatus-appropriate-inspiration-for-an-exalted-character?p=1444121#post1444121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third Edition has softened that somewhat.<br /> <br /> It no longer requires a single driving goal at the core of the character replacing it with the concept of Essence Fever which is essentially that not using charms/essence isn't like being a wizard who can choose not to casting spells but more like an athlete who doesn't want to use their muscles. So you can disband your army and return to the farm until you're needed but if trouble comes near you you're probably not going to want to keep your head down because ultimately your essence wants to be used.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Although Essence Fever is also supposed to be a thing that older Exalted have an effective handle on.<br /> <br /> We're talking about characters who are capable of living somewhere between three hundred and five thousand years. If somebody spends six times the typical mortal lifetime engaging in intrigue and adventure and then wants to take a rest for some fifty to sixty years, their patron isn't going to come down and chide them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T13:54:04-07:00","id":1444385,"title":"","content":"If Leviathan can go play Achilles in his tent for a thousand years in a bout of melancholy after failing to save his mate I'm pretty sure it is perfectly okay for an exalt to humbly step down from a position of administrative power to go do other things after accomplishing their task instead of clinging to that position for the sake of power itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T14:13:47-07:00","id":1444389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444062-cincinnatus-appropriate-inspiration-for-an-exalted-character?p=1444385#post1444385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Leviathan can go play Achilles in his tent for a thousand years in a bout of melancholy after failing to save his mate I'm pretty sure it is perfectly okay for an exalt to humbly step down from a position of administrative power to go do other things after accomplishing their task instead of clinging to that position for the sake of power itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Leviathan doesn't quite count because he's still been an active guardian against other things in the depths. Just not governing Luthe and not taking the fight to the Dragon Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T15:39:07-07:00","id":1444395,"title":"","content":"I don't think Luthe saw enough trouble for him to count as an active guardian, its geography pretty harshly limits the number of people that can attack it in force even if they wanted to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T16:15:33-07:00","id":1444398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444062-cincinnatus-appropriate-inspiration-for-an-exalted-character?p=1444395#post1444395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Luthe saw enough trouble for him to count as an active guardian, its geography pretty harshly limits the number of people that can attack it in force even if they wanted to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure there are other threats down there that aren't, strictly speaking, people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T17:04:25-07:00","id":1444409,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure that if he had been regularly defending an important strategic resource of the silver pact from serious threats he wouldn't have developed a reputation as a lazy do nothing with people like the Black Lion. The book is pretty clear that he hasn't been doing anything worth noting and this waste of potential power is why a lot of other Lunars are mad at him. I don't know why you are insistent on pretending that Achilles was totally doing something important in his tent but he wasn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T17:55:39-07:00","id":1444414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444062-cincinnatus-appropriate-inspiration-for-an-exalted-character?p=1444395#post1444395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Luthe saw enough trouble for him to count as an active guardian, its geography pretty harshly limits the number of people that can attack it in force even if they wanted to.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a trench with the Wyld at the bottom of it that the western edge of the city is continuously crumbling into. There is a city made from ship wreckage inhabited by ghosts and criminal exiles from Luthe that deals in spying and assassination. There is a city of holy spires left over from the Niobraran League ruled over by religious zealots who keep trying to attack Luthe's temple district; Leviathan is specifically referenced as having assisted in fighting off the incursions from that last one.<br /> <br /> It's Fangs at the Gate. If it's going to bother including a location in the Undersea, it's going to make the environment down there interesting. An environment that might produce, say, rival nations that would make war upon a city-state of particular size and prosperity.<br /> <br /> I mean, the ocean is limiting? Great White Sharks annually make journeys of up to 20,000 km. There's no animal on land that can travel like that. Do you not think the ocean of <b>Exalted</b> might contain any interesting giant benthic monsters to menace a large gathering of meat creatures were there not an ancient martial demigod in residence?<br /> <br /> Also, he's described as having been a guardian for Pact members who sought refuge in his city, who might be presumed to bring some of their problems home with them, Wyld Hunt or otherwise, even if the greater forces of the Shogunate never encroached upon him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure if he had been regularly defending an important strategic resource of the silver pact from serious threats he wouldn't have developed a reputation as a lazy do nothing with people like the Black Lion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The person like what is the Black Lion is the Silver Pact's big advocate for abandoning the asymmetrical stuff and waging direct war, he's not very happy with defensive anything. Sha'a Oka is also very particularly hung up on fighting against the Shogunate in particular, which can be taken as meaning he would be unimpressed with a Lunar fighting anything other than that foe.<br /> <br /> I mean, the Black Lion is... a bit of a weirdo. I don't think we're meant to take his outlook on anything as having all of its ducks in a row.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The book is pretty clear that he hasn't been doing anything worth noting</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> The things I have pointed to above in combination with the book consistently referring to him as Luthe's protector, widely venerated as a guardian deity, are the basis of why I find this incorrect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">this waste of potential power is why a lot of other Lunars are mad at him.</div> </div> </div> </div>About two Lunars are described as being mad at him. That is to be compared to the statement that most Lunars regard his prior absence in terms of not knowing what to make of him, the other First Age elders recalling him with fondness and respect, and the several followers he is given that not only includes people who are adherents of other shahan-yas, but one or two who are actually in league with Sha'a Oka.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T19:50:08-07:00","id":1444432,"title":"","content":"And while he was sulking in his tent Achilles asked his mother to curse the shit out of the Achaeans (his allies, for the record) and got his wish. Being Achilles in his tent doesn't mean doing <i>literally</i> nothing at all as you sit around refusing to provide the considerable amount of aid you are capable of thanks to some sort of emotional hangup. Seriously, Leviathan is an ancient god like being who can probably single handedly sink armadas. Saying that he he sometimes fights a damn shark or some randos squatting in Niobraran ruins who swim too close to him doesn't cut it as meaningful activity for a being of that scale. If anything some of the things you have listed to defend Leviathan are actually just further proof of how he hasn't even been defending Luthe to his fullest and just sort of floated around occasionally eating anything stupid enough to metaphorically swim up to him and slap him in the face.<br /> <br /> Luthe hasn't even realized that Wyld zone is a thing (they think its just ocean pressure and such, that is why the efforts they make to counter the crumbling fail. They are misunderstanding the problem and therefore not using the proper solutiong) so Leviathan isn't doing anything to guard against it, for example. Similarly he has done nothing about Galbadan because, as the text makes clear, Luthe hasn't realized it is a murderous den of evil (apparently spies and such are good at pretending they aren't). By mentioning them you do nothing but provide evidence that Leviathan was no active guardian working to keep Luthe safe. His defense showed about as much proactive drive as a pressure plate trigger trap that sits there doing nothing at all until someone literally steps on it. Except a trap would be more reliable since sometimes Leviathan doesn't even do that (the text says he didn't help with all the raids launched by the ruin squatters out of the Obsidian city).<br /> <br /> Seriously, the guy basically exists to show that Exalts can go off and do not epic things for awhile instead of being uncontrollably compelled by their exaltation to go 'be awesome' and you shouldn't hesitate to have your character go be 'boring' for awhile if it fits them and the story. They also exist to show that Exalts are heroes in the old Greek sense, they are awesome at what they do but they are still ultimately human and therefore flawed (and thanks to their scope these flaws can result in some truly spectacular things beyond the capability of regular humans like a depressive fugue state lasting for centuries).<br /> <br /> Honestly, I like Leviathan. As someone who had untreated chronic depression for awhile I can completely empathize with someone finding themselves just so completely done with life's garbage that doing much of anything is a titanic struggle. It is just to Leviathan's great misfortune that various factors meant they never really got treatment for it (the rub about that kind of soul crushing haze is that it tends to make someone unlikely to seek treatment themselves instead of needing to be pushed into it by outside interference).<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, this is literally the first sentence of the section on Leviathan's relationship with the pact. &quot;Leviathan has few political allies within the Pact for<br /> a shahan-ya of his age, and still labors at forging such connections.&quot;. He is mostly liked by other old people who knew him before he got depression and struggles to get much respect from the 'whimper snappers' who have only ever known him as that whale dude who spends his time floating around Luthe being a stage hazard to the occasional attackers. Don't let your perception be skewed by his write up and Luthe mostly mentioning people that interact with him. Thats like calling the Scarlet Dynasty popular based on all those dynasts in The Realm liking it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 04-18-2021, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}